<section class="trust band" id="questions">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="shead" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;text-align:center;justify-items:center;gap:8px">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow" data-rv>Before you write</p>
        <h2 class="h2" data-rv style="--d:60ms;max-width:none">Six things people ask first.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="trust__dek" data-rv style="--d:100ms;max-width:none">Answered here so you don’t have to spend an email
      on them. <b>The pricing one is a real number, not a range designed to get you on a call.</b></p>
    </div>
    <div class="qas" data-rv style="--d:140ms"><details class="qa2"><summary class="qa2__q">How fast do you actually reply?<i></i></summary><p class="qa2__a">Inside a day for hiring teams, two for candidates. If it’s urgent, say so in the first line and it moves to the top.</p></details><details class="qa2"><summary class="qa2__q">What does it cost?<i></i></summary><p class="qa2__a">Fifteen to twenty per cent per hire, no setup fee and no retainer. You pay when someone starts. Volume and RPO shapes are priced differently and we’ll walk you through it on the call.</p></details><details class="qa2"><summary class="qa2__q">Is there ever a fee for candidates?<i></i></summary><p class="qa2__a">No. Not now, not when you’re placed, not ever.</p></details><details class="qa2"><summary class="qa2__q">Do you work outside India?<i></i></summary><p class="qa2__a">Yes. We run mandates for GCCs and global teams hiring into India, and for India-based teams hiring elsewhere. Our people sit in Pune and Bengaluru.</p></details><details class="qa2"><summary class="qa2__q">Can you handle remote and hybrid roles?<i></i></summary><p class="qa2__a">Yes, and the bar is set differently for them, and remote roles weight written communication and self-direction more heavily, and we’ll say so in the rubric.</p></details><details class="qa2"><summary class="qa2__q">What should I put in the message?<i></i></summary><p class="qa2__a">The role, the level, how long it’s been open and what you have already tried. Four sentences is plenty. We would rather have the honest version than a polished brief.</p></details></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap band close" id="contact">
  <div class="shead" style="grid-template-columns:1fr;text-align:center;justify-items:center;gap:8px">
